# 🔌 Drovi Socket.IO Testing Guide

> **For mobile app developers:** This guide explains every socket event in Drovi, how to connect, and how to test each one using simple tools.

---

## 📡 Architecture Overview

Drovi uses **2 WebSocket namespaces** (think of them as 2 separate socket connections):

| Namespace | URL | Who Uses It |
|---|---|---|
| `/orders` | `ws://YOUR_SERVER:3001/orders` | Admin dashboard, Restaurant/Shop dashboard, Customer app, Rider app |
| `/rider-location` | `ws://YOUR_SERVER:3001/rider-location` | Rider app (GPS tracking), Admin dashboard (live map) |

---

## 🧪 How to Test (Step by Step)

### Tool: Use **Postman** (has Socket.IO support) or any Socket.IO test client

#### Option 1: Postman (Recommended)
1. Open Postman → New → Socket.IO Request
2. Enter URL: `ws://localhost:3001/orders` or `ws://localhost:3001/rider-location`
3. Under "Settings", set transport to `websocket`
4. Click **Connect**
5. You can now emit events and listen for responses

#### Option 2: Simple HTML Test Page
Save this as `test.html` and open in browser:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Drovi Socket Tester</title></head>
<body>
<h1>Drovi Socket Tester</h1>
<pre id="log" style="background:#111;color:#0f0;padding:20px;height:500px;overflow:auto;"></pre>

<script src="https://cdn.socket.io/4.7.2/socket.io.min.js"></script>
<script>
function log(msg) {
  document.getElementById('log').textContent += new Date().toLocaleTimeString() + ' | ' + msg + '\n';
  document.getElementById('log').scrollTop = document.getElementById('log').scrollHeight;
}

// ==========================================
// CHANGE THESE VALUES FOR YOUR TEST
// ==========================================
const SERVER = 'http://localhost:3001';
const NAMESPACE = '/orders';  // or '/rider-location'

const socket = io(SERVER + NAMESPACE, {
  transports: ['websocket', 'polling'],
});

socket.on('connect', () => log('✅ CONNECTED! Socket ID: ' + socket.id));
socket.on('disconnect', (reason) => log('❌ DISCONNECTED: ' + reason));
socket.on('connect_error', (err) => log('❌ ERROR: ' + err.message));

// Listen to ALL events (very useful for debugging)
socket.onAny((event, ...args) => {
  log('📨 EVENT: ' + event + ' → ' + JSON.stringify(args));
});

// === EXPOSE FUNCTIONS TO BROWSER CONSOLE ===
window.socket = socket;
window.emit = (event, data) => {
  socket.emit(event, data, (response) => {
    log('📬 RESPONSE for ' + event + ': ' + JSON.stringify(response));
  });
};

log('🔌 Connecting to ' + SERVER + NAMESPACE + '...');
</script>

<h3>Open browser console (F12) and use:</h3>
<pre style="background:#eee;padding:10px;">
// Register as admin:
emit('register_admin', { userId: 'YOUR_USER_ID' })

// Register as customer:
emit('register_customer', { customerId: 'YOUR_USER_ID' })

// Register as rider:
emit('register_rider', { riderId: 'YOUR_USER_ID' })

// Register as vendor:
emit('register_vendor', { vendorType: 'restaurant', vendorId: 'YOUR_RESTAURANT_ID' })

// Subscribe to order updates:
emit('subscribe_to_order', { orderId: 'ORDER_ID', customerId: 'YOUR_USER_ID' })

// Ping test:
emit('ping', {})
</pre>
</body>
</html>
```

